error-payload.js: toRunErrorRawEvent keeps the provider's HTTP status next to
the body it forwards, forwards an AWS service exception's name, fault side
and status (it has no body), and forwards the status alone when the error has
no body. `code` precedence (#985) is unchanged.
Upstream: to be raised as an issue (a status field on RUN_ERROR).
Remove when a @tanstack/ai release carries the status on RUN_ERROR.

